.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Debye and Hückel (1923) showed that each ion&#x27;s cloud of counter-ions lowers its activity below its concentration, by an amount growing with ionic strength and ionic charge. This example uses nernst_potential_with_activity (built on chemistrykit.solutions.systems.activity) to show how the potential of a Cu2+/Cu electrode drifts away from the ideal Nernst value as the solution gets more concentrated, and that the correction vanishes in the dilute limit.">

